\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dollar Higher Despite Japan MOF Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 03:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was stronger at midday in Tokyo Monday compared with its levels earlier in the session, as Japanese corporate customers shrugged off dollar-negative comments from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  As reported, Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the ministry's international finance bureau, told a small group of reporters he 'doesn't accept' a further weakening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda was also asked about comments made eight days ago by Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at the ministry. Sakakibara said Dec. 28 that the ministry was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a 'surprising' extent as needed. \par \par \uc2  Asked if that sentiment still holds true, Kuroda said, 'That's exactly right.' \par \par \uc2  But traders said such comments are becoming mundane. \par \par \uc2  'Saying things like that has become his routine job. Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  like that isn't going to have any effect,' said a trader at a French bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The trader added that actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also not likely to be effective, because \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weak economic fundamentals -- in contrast to the strong U.S. economy --  are working against the Bank of Japan's efforts to boost the yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT (9:15 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading at Y132.40, up from Y132.18 around 0040 GMT (7:40 p.m. EST) and unchanged from Y132.40 in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.7995, higher than DM1.7985 earlier in Tokyo and below DM1.8045 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0230GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du150028a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
