\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Speculation Of BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Eases \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1997\par 23:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Also pressuring the pound was a report that mortgage lending in the U.K. fell by 7.9% to 3.787 billion GBP in November. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar extended the gains it posted Monday against the mark to reach an intraday high of DM1.7969 at 1102 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was a 123-point rise in the Dow Jones Industrial Average and some earlier dovish comments from Deutsche Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer. \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer said he considered monetary stability in Germany to be 'relatively good' and that the import price inflation had slowed, remarks which traders said suggested the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be raising interest rates soon. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a report that the U.S. conference board's consumer confidence index surged to 134.5 in December from 128.1 in November provided fresh evidence of a robust U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  With Tokyo financial markets closed for the New Year holiday until January 5, speculation eased that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to defend the beleaguered yen. \par \par \uc2  Rumors had circulated last week that the BOJ could exploit the thin Christmas market to inexpensively drive up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With that threat virtually removed, the dollar was allowed to creep back above Y130.00 Tuesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Canadian dollar recovered somewhat from its recent weakness against the dollar. Late in New York, the U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4324, down from C$1.4395 late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 30-12-97 \par \par \uc2  2222GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcu0a0ql\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
