\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup-2: Speculative Dlr Buying Seen Next Week \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 1997\par 07:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar is likely to see speculative buying next week as Japanese corporate players leave for the New Year's holiday and overseas hedge funds come back from the Christmas holiday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Key considerations next week will be whether the dollar will be pushed up for a test of Y131.56, the recent high posted on Dec. 15, and whether the BOJ will enter the market again within the year. \par \par \uc2  'If the dollar keeps trading at the Y130.00-level, it will be quite easy to break through the recent high,' the U.S. bank dealer said. If that happens, the dollar could easily rise as high as Y131 or Y132, which would almost certainly compel \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers pointed to the BOJ's lack of success last week in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, and some said the BOJ is unlikely to enter the market again until next year. The dollar fell as low as Y125.85 on Dec. 17 after the BOJ sold dollars following a surprise announcement by Prime Minister Ryutato Hashimoto of a Y2 trillion income tax cut. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since crept up more than Y4. \par \par \uc2  There is some speculation in the market that Hashimoto will call for further tax cuts as part of a fourth economic stimulus package in January. The BOJ may hold off on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again until such a package is announced, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Unless such an economic plan emerges, 'BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be far less effective (than it was last week),' the U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  However, recent remarks by Hashimoto seem to invalidate rumors that more tax cuts are in the works. Hashimoto was quoted as saying Thursday that he's confident economic recovery will resume as a result of the government's recent economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0622GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcq09ygh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
