\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Japan Faces Conflicting Forces: Weak Yen, Low Rates \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikako Mogi \par \uc2  Staff Reporter \par \uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par 14:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week to prop up the yen are likely to have a limited impact, as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to keep interest rates low to prevent a further meltdown in the economy, analysts said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to pursue contradictory goals - stopping the yen from collapsing with yen purchases in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market while keeping interest rates down with massive injections of liquidity into the money markets, analysts added. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week soon after the government announced a surprise 2 trillion yen ($15.5 billion) cut in income taxes. The initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was extremely effective, pushing down the dollar by nearly six yen to a low last week of 125.85 yen. But the dollar has since recovered to trade late Wednesday in Asia around 130.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan has to keep domestic interest rates as low as possible to counter worries about further failures of Japanese financial institutions - fears which have driven up money market rates and threatened to disrupt the smooth flow of funds. \par \par \uc2  "The effect of the dollar selling, yen buying is logically limited," Yasuhide Yahiro, associate director at Bear Stearns (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) Ltd., said. "The only way the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can succeed (in strengthening the yen) is when interest rates are raised. That's totally out of question for Japan." \par \par \uc2  As a result, analysts suspect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be somewhat half-hearted, with the financial authorities mostly concerned to prevent an abrupt collapse in the yen - as opposed to a gentle weakening - and to head off U.S. criticisms that Japan is using a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to export its way out of financial crisis and economic malaise. \par \par \uc2  The authorities may also have wanted to send a signal to the markets at a time when yen weakness threatened to cause further selling in the troubled Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the South Korean won, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But the bigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  priority is to keep interest rates low, analysts said. "When monetary policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy are going in opposite directions - yen liquidity rising in the money markets while it is absorbed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - one or the other must be wrong," Ryutaro Kono, senior economist at Dai-Ichi Life Research Institute, said. "If \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy doesn't match economic fundamentals, it's wrong. The yen steadily weakened as economic prospects deteriorated. A weak yen is consistent with economic fundamentals," he added. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Bank of Japan officials are eager to reject speculation that they were changing their money-market-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy last week to bolster the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the money markets by absorbing excess funds early in the session, sending overnight call rates shooting higher. And on Thrusday, the Bank of Japan drained funds at around the time it was rumored to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen. Earlier that day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had announced an outright purchase of bonds to cap the rise in long-term market rates. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official expressed dismay at speculation that the Bank of Japan was allowing market rates to rise in order to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He emphasized the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overwhelming desire to keep interest rates low in the money markets to ensure abundant liquidity and lessen the effects of a credit crunch pinching Japanese corporate borrowers. \par \par \uc2  "It must have been trying times for the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) when they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Mikio Wakatsuki, chairman of the board of counselors at Japan Research Institute and a former senior official at the Bank of Japan. He said call money rates weren't rising because of any effect from yen purchases by the Bank of Japan in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Rather, the growing credit crunch is forcing rates up even in the face of massive money market injections by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Another reason for skepticism about the effects on the yen of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's admission that the economy is relying heavily on a weakened yen to stimulate exports and support the flagging economy. \par \par \uc2  In its latest monthly report released Monday, the Bank of Japan admitted that economic growth "has stalled." Masayuki Matsushima, director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's research department, said later that given the yen's current level, exports will continue to give underlying support to the economy. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1997 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  1138 4131 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020011006dtco016j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
