\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up vs yen in Tokyo, new MOF measures ignored. \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0300 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     130.26/29\tab \tab    130.33-129.50\par  USD/DEM     1.7758/60\tab \tab    1.7769-1.7723\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against the yen by midday on Wednesday in thin Tokyo trade, with the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  receiving little help from new measures announced by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) aimed at correcting banks' restrained lending stance. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's upside was heavy due to fears of possible dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  "The MOF measures on the PCA system and the ruling party's measures on preferred stocks failed to move Tokyo stocks significantly. So the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market chose to ignore them," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  The MOF said in a statement on Wednesday that it would make its "prompt corrective action" (PCA) system for banks operating domestically more flexible in response to restrained lending practices by banks. \par \par \uc2  The PCA system, which takes effect from April next year, uses capital adequacy ratios as a gauge of the soundness of financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtco00o6m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
