\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank of Japan Watch/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Create Two-Way Mkt For Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par 09:07\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "It must have been trying times for the BOJ when they\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," said Mikio Wakatsuki,\par chairman of the board of counselors at Japan Research\par Institute and a former senior official at the Bank of Japan.\par He said call money rates weren't rising because of any\par effect from yen purchases by the Bank of Japan in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. Rather, the growing credit crunch is\par forcing rates up even in the face of massive money market\par injections by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Another reason for skepticism about the effects on the\par yen of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par admission that the Japanese economy is currently relying\par heavily on yen weakness to stimulate exports and support the\par flagging economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In its latest monthly report released Monday, the Bank\par of Japan admitted that Japan's economic growth "has\par stalled." Masayuki Matsushima, director of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's research department, said later that given the\par current level of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, Japan's exports\par will continue to give underlying support to the economy.\par    It was rather the perception in the markets that there\par was a "one-way bet" in selling yen that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par the finance ministry wanted to counter last week.\par    "For \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authoritites, it's seriously troubling to\par see market expectations all pointing to one direction,"\par Wakatsuki said. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inverventions were a gimmick\par to play up the risks, to make market participants wake up to\par the very basics of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market - that there are\par always two-way changes and there's always uncertainty."\par    The effect of the yen buying was magnified by the\par surprise announcement of the tax cut plan last week, which\par had already sent the dollar tumbling.\par    Yahiro at Bear Stearns also pointed to the political\par dimension - fears in Tokyo that the U.S. will renew its\par complaints about yen weakness if the trade surplus continues\par to widen.\par    And Japan is also concerned that a plunging yen is only\par adding to the turmoil in Asian financial markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  12-24-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0307EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtco02qcl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
