\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank of Japan Watch/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Priority Keeping Rates Low \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par 09:01\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    But the bigger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  priority is to keep interest\par rates low, analysts said.\par    "When monetary policy and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy are going in\par opposite directions - yen liquidity rising in the money\par markets while it is absorbed in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par - one or the other must be wrong," said Ryutaro Kono, senior\par economist at Dai-Ichi Life Research Institute.\par    "If \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy doesn't match economic fundamentals,\par it's wrong. The yen steadily weakened as economic prospects\par deteriorated. A weak yen is consistent with economic\par fundamentals."\par    Indeed, Bank of Japan officials are keen to reject\par speculation that they were changing their money market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy last week to bolster the effect of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Last Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the money\par markets by absorbing excess funds early in the session,\par sending overnight call rates shooting higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  And on\par Thrusday, the Bank of Japan drained funds at around the time\par it was rumored to be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yen. Earlier\par that day, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had announced an outright\par purchase of bonds to cap the rise in long-term market rates.\par    One \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official expressed dismay at\par speculation that the Bank of Japan was allowing market rates\par to rise in order to bolster the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . He\par emphasized the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's overwhelming desire to keep\par interest rates low in the money markets to ensure liquidity\par is abundant and lessen the effects of a credit crunch that\par is affecting Japanese corporate borrowers.\par    In fact, the Bank of Japan has taken every conceivable\par steps to ensure liquidity is ample in the money markets ever\par since late November, when a series of major financial\par failures occured. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has boosted the amount of\par regular outright bond purchases to Y200 billion each from\par Y100 billion; and it bought bonds via repurchase agreements\par (RP's) that will be unwound in the new fiscal year that\par starts April 1 - an unusual step to ensure funding is smooth\par for the fiscal year-end as well. The BOJ also in effect left\par massive excessive reserves in the banking system on the last\par day of the recent monthly accumulation period - when\par reserves have traditionally evened out with the requirement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  12-24-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0301EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtco02qch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
