\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Watch: Low Rates Counter  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikako Mogi \par \uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par 08:52\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets last week to prop up the yen are likely\par to have a limited impact, as long as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs\par to keep interest rates low to prevent a further meltdown in\par the economy, analysts say.\par    The Bank of Japan has been forced to pursue two\par contradictory goals - stopping the yen from collapsing with\par yen purchases in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market while keeping interest\par rates down with massive injections of yen liquidity into the\par money markets, the analysts say.\par    The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week soon\par after the government announced a surprise Y2 trillion cut in\par income tax. The initial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was extremely\par effective, pushing down the dollar by nearly six yen to a\par low last week of Y125.85. But the dollar has since recovered\par to trade late Wednesday in Asia around Y130.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Bank of Japan has to keep domestic interest rates as\par low as possible to counter the fears about further failures\par of Japanese financial institutions - fears which have driven\par up money market rates and threatened to disrupt the smooth\par flow of funds.\par    "The effect of the dollar selling, yen buying is\par logically limited," says Yasuhide Yahiro, associate director\par at Bear Stearns (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) Ltd. "The only way the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can succeed (in strengthening the yen) is when\par interest rates are raised. That's totally out of question\par for Japan."\par    As a result, analysts suspect the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be somewhat half-hearted,\par with the financial authorities mostly concerned to prevent\par an abrupt collapse in the yen - as opposed to a gentle\par weakening - and to head off U.S. criticisms that Japan is using\par a weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to export its way out of financial crisis.\par    The authorities may also have wanted to send a signal to\par the markets at a time when yen weakness threatened to cause\par further selling in the troubled Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the\par South Korean won, analysts say.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  12-24-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0252EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1138 4131 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtco02qcc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
