\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Shrugs Off Data, News In Thin Trading \b0\par\par\uc2  By Marianne Sullivan \par \uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1997\par 22:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The signs pointed clearly in the direction of a stronger dollar Tuesday, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders didn't follow them. \par \par \uc2  Events and statistics which normally would have pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher had little effect with few major participants active in thin markets ahead of the winter holidays. Japanese markets were closed Tuesday in celebration of the Emperor's birthday, further limiting volume. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar had difted lower against the Deutsche mark and fallen back against the yen compared with day-earlier levels, traders said, describing Tuesday's session as lackluster. \par \par \uc2  Reports of record-high durable good orders and higher-than-expected corporate profits once again underlined the strength of the U.S. economy. At the same time, more bad news poured out of Asia as new downgrades for South Korea's ratings sent the won tumbling 12.5% to an all-time low against the dollar while Japan's Nikkei lost another 3.4%. \par \par \uc2  But traders were closing the books for 1997 and unwilling to make bold moves. Said one dealer when asked what the market was watching on Tuesday: 'The clock.' \par \par \uc2  'People are afraid to hold long dollar/yen positions going into the holidays,' said Marc Chandler, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in New York. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the holidays offer the ideal conditions for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid very low volume with many players out of the markets. \par \par \uc2  'There's a lot of speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday,' said John Hanly, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank Austria in New York. \par \par \uc2  Rumors of planned rescue measures in South Korea and Japan sparked a yen buying spree mid-afternoon in New York. Speculation was ripe that the Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would announce a relaxation of capital adequacy rules which could alleviate a credit crunch. Other traders reported rumors of an additional rescue plan for Korea, coordinated by major economic powers or international financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted DM1.7745 late in New York, up from DM1.7810 late Monday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at Y129.33, down from Y130.13. Sterling was trading at $1.6675 from $1.6635 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-12-97 \par \par \uc2  2144GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 2217GMT) \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcn09x6z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
