\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up in late Tokyo amid lack of BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0720 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0700 GMT\par  USD/JPY     130.32/37\tab \tab 130.75-129.13\par  USD/DEM     1.7817/22\tab \tab 1.7848-1.7757\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The dollar rose sharply against the yen by late Tokyo on Monday amid a lack of dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market had been reluctant to push the dollar too aggressively due to fears that the BOJ might step in to sell dollars between 129.50 and 130 yen. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained absent despite the dollar's rise above 130 yen. \par \par \uc2  Stop-loss dollar buying orders were triggered above 130 yen, briefly taking the greenback to the day's high of 130.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  Buying was initiated by overseas players, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A bout of profit-taking pared some of the greenback's gains, but it remained firmly above 130 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ may have chosen to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point because it would not be very effective until more dollar long positions build up. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ is believed to have spent a total of around $10 billion last week to brake the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's falls. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had initially helped knock the dollar nearly six yen lower on Wednesday but its impact waned by Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar demand from Japanese investors is just overwhelming. The dollar's rise may be unstoppable by BOJ action alone," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Unless the U.S. Federal Reserve and European central banks join the BOJ in a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar is likely to continue climbing," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar demand would remain strong in coming days because more new investment trust funds are expected to be established later this week. \par \par \uc2  The yen came under more pressure in the afternoon as the key Nikkei 225 stock average fell below the psychologically important 15,000 level. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei ended down 515.49 points, or 3.37 percent, at 14,799.40, after falling as low as 14,569.43. \par \par \uc2  "After the failure of Toshoku last week, there are fears that more companies could go bust," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Foodstuffs trader Toshoku Ltd applied for protection under Japanese bankruptcy laws at Tokyo District Court last Thursday with debts of 528.9 billion yen and debt guarantees of 110.9 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  Stricter lending policies by banks were partly blamed for the company's failure. \par \par \uc2  "There is a vicious circle. Bankruptcies make banks more reluctant to lend, which in turn could trigger more failures," said a Japanese bank dealer. "In such a situation, one would be hesitant to buy the yen." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, commercial dollar buying at the 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing and talk of dollar purchases relating to securities investments helped the dollar firm, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sporadic dollar buying from Japanese importers was also detected, they said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said activity by Tokyo players was generally slow ahead of a market holiday here on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's financial markets will be closed on Tuesday in celebration of the Emperor's birthday. \par \par \uc2  The greenback also rose against the mark in tandem with its gains versus the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 129.35/45 yen and 1.7765/75 marks in New York on Friday. (( Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-9780 email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcm00u74\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
