\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr higher vs yen in late Tokyo on Nikkei's fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0610 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     129.83/93\tab \tab 129.90-129.13\par  USD/DEM     1.7833/38\tab \tab 1.7848-1.7757\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against the yen by late afternoon Tokyo on Monday, following a fall in the key Nikkei 225 stock average below the psychologically important 15,000 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But operators were reluctant to buy dollars too aggressively due to worries about possible dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still bullish about the dollar and bearish about the yen. But most people were hesitant to trade actively ahead of a holiday in Tokyo," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's financial markets will be closed on Tuesday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar slowly crept higher in thin trade, following a sharp fall in Tokyo stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei ended down 515.49 points, or 3.37 percent, at 14,799.40, after falling as low as 14,569.43. \par \par \uc2  "After the failure of Toshoku last week, there are fears that more companies could go bust," said the trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Foodstuffs trader Toshoku Ltd applied for protection under Japanese bankruptcy laws at Tokyo District Court last Thursday with debts of 528.9 billion yen and debt guarantees of 110.9 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  Banks' stricter lending attitudes were partly blamed for the company's failure. \par \par \uc2  "There is a vicious circle. Bankruptcies make banks more reluctant to lend, which in turn could trigger more failures," said a Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Under such a situation, one would be hesitant to buy the yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the BOJ to prevent the dollar from going above 130 yen, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't been detected in the market as of 6:50 GMT Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ may have spent around $10 billion last week to brake the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's falls. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had initially helped knock the dollar nearly six yen lower on Wednesday, but its impact waned by Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar demand from Japanese investors is just overwhelming. The dollar's rise may be unstoppable by BOJ action alone," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Unless the U.S. Federal Reserve and European central banks join the BOJ in a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar is likely to continue climbing," the city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar demand would remain strong in the coming days, as more new investment trust funds are expected to be established later this week. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, dollar buying by commercial interests at the 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing and talk of dollar purchases relating to securities investments helped the dollar firm, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sporadic dollar buying from Japanese importers was also detected, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later extended gains on buying by overseas players in late Tokyo as stop-loss buy orders were triggered around 130 yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ may be choosing not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now as it would not be very effective unless more longs build up, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was also higher against the mark in tandem with its gains versus the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 129.35/45 yen and 1.7765/75 marks in New York on Friday. (( Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-9780 email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcm00u72\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
