\par\par \b \uc2  Yen malaise depresses Asian regional  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1997\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 19 (Reuters) - The yen's failure to extend its rise, despite Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , put paid to any further gains in Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drifted lower in listless year-end markets as the yen failed to make much headway against the dollar following the boost it got from a surprise economic stimulus package on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BoJ spent between $4.0 and $5.0 supporting the yen, surpassing the estimated $3.0 billion it spent on Wednesday in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since August 1992. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won's limp response to the election of opposition leader Kim Dae-jung as the country's new president also weighed on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The won weakened to a late 1,570.0 to the dollar against Wednesday's 1,481.0 close. Korean financial markets were closed for the presidential election on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Mounting dollar demand from importers for end-week settlements depressed the won, but dealers and analysts said the market was also concerned about Kim's commitment to IMF reforms. \par \par \uc2  "The key thing is, is he going to be the people's man or the IMF's man?" said Jimmy Koh, regional economist at I.D.E.A. in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "On the one hand he's promised to comply with IMF reforms. On the other hand, he's been promising voters that unemployment will be capped. But we know that's never possible," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the general gloom, Japan's promise of a 165 billion yen bridge loan to help Seoul meet a mountain of short-term debt only reminded traders that South Korea's reserves are dwindling. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar recovered from opening lows, but remained weak at T$32.311 to the U.S. dollar against Thursday's T$32.200 close as movements in the yen and won dictated its direction. \par \par \uc2  "The Taiwan dollar has been dancing closely to the beat of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "We will especially follow movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Japan, South Korea and Singapore, which have direct and tough competition with Taiwan in exports," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar closed locally at 7.7492/7.7502 to the U.S. dollar, compared with Thursday's close of 7.7475/85, and forwards firmed in the wake of declines in the yen and won. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, the Thai baht slid to 46.00 to the dollar onshore from 45.05 on Thursday evening. \par \par \uc2  The offshore rate was sharply lower at 45.05, against 43.75/44.25, its drop exaggerated by very poor liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said weakness in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and renewed corporate demand for dollars after two days of gains in the baht were working against the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Thai Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda, on a visit to Tokyo, said he had asked Japanese banks to extend their present credit lines to Thai firms. \par \par \uc2  He said it was not a request for fresh loans but rather a rolling over of present credits. \par \par \uc2  Tarrin was also quoted by a Japanese Finance Ministry official as saying Thailand would like to have more loans denominated in yen rather than in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah slipped back below the level of 5,000 to the dollar after perking up on Thursday as a public appearance by President Suharto calmed market fears about his health. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah was shaken by Standard and Poor's downgrade of three Indonesian companies. \par \par \uc2  Ample swap cash-flows in Singapore were also making dollar holdings attractive. "You pay small costs for speculating on wild swings. This is a factor undermining the rupiah," said one. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar edged up to 1.6655 to the U.S. dollar after languishing below the 1.67 level all morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said interbank rates had come off a bit, triggering speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had added liquidity to the money market to depress domestic interest rates. \par \par \uc2  A sharp spike up in interbank rates this week has raised expectations that local banks would be forced to raise lending rates again, a move that would further depress Singapore's already soft property market, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit eased to 3.8400 to the U.S. dollar from 3.7850 late on Thursday, but dealers said dollar-selling interest above the 3.85 level would limit its decline. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was at 39.25 to the dollar against Thursday's 39.69 close. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcj00rkc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
