\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday:Dlr Continues Up Vs. Yen On Position Squaring \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1997\par 03:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar continues edging up against the yen in Tokyo midday Thursday, as overseas hedge funds and Japanese importers buy dollars for position squaring. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, however, eased slightly against the Deutsche mark as traders bought marks ahead of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's meeting later Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are engaging mainly in position adjustment in the Thursday morning Tokyo session after the dollar-selling binge Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Although the Y2 trillion tax cut decision by the Japanese government and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday have restored some confidence in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar-bullish sentiment still remains basically intact, traders noted. \par \par \uc2  'A one-way rise of the yen from here is unthinkable,' said a trader at a Japanese city bank. 'The Japanese economy is likely to remain stagnant, while the U.S. economy continues its sustained healthy growth,' the trader explained. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar's upside remains capped around Y127.50 for fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese side, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (9:00 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading at Y127.45, up from Y127.25 around 0030 GMT (7:30 p.m. EST) and above Y127.13 in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at Y127.50 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.7755, slightly lower than DM1.7760 earlier in Tokyo an