\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Rupiah Rises On Suharto's Appearance \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1997\par 07:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y71.76, up from Y71.39 in New York late Wednesday and above Y71.69 in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6510, slightly down from $1.6512 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6508 in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that it's difficult to maintain long dollar positions as the U.S. and European markets wind down the year and the markets become increasingly thin. They said in addition to being the holiday season, it appears to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  season, so the market will remain wary through the rest of December. \par \par \uc2  However, most market participants said that the medium- to long-term trend still favors a dollar rise versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  Comments by a former senior official at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday added to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Makoto Utsumi, formerly vice minister for international affairs at the ministry and now a professor, said in an interview with Nikkei News Service that there remains a possibility that the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will carry out coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to drive the dollar lower. \par \par \uc2  'Both countries would basically have no problem with the dollar between Y110 and Y120,' Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Asia, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stable and mainly higher versus the dollar. The Indonesian rupiah rose after the first public appearance of Indonesian President Suharto Thursday in two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah, which had plummeted on rumors that the 76-year-old head of state was seriously ill, climbed to 5,200 rupiah at 0545 GMT (12:45 a.m. EST) against the dollar, compared with its close Wednesday at 5,550 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore spot market for the Thai baht, the dollar was weaker at 42.80 baht at 0541 GMT, down from 46.25 baht late Wednesday. The baht was helped by the stronger regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won wasn't traded Thursday, as markets were closed for the presidential election. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0653GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtci09pn8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
