\par\par \b \uc2  Japan BOJ Seen Generous Fri; Key Rate Likely Under 0.40% \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1997\par 00:39\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan is expected to keep\par its generous money market stance Friday, leaving reserves\par between Y500 billion and Y1 trillion above the requirement at\par its usual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  time at 0020 GMT Friday (7:20 p.m. EST\par Thursday), traders said.\par    The key unsecured rate for overnight call money will\par likely be kept under 0.40%, with the weighted average around\par 0.35%, traders said. The weighted average Thursday was 0.36%.\par    The Bank of Japan left Y500 billion of reserves above the\par requirement for the second straight session Thursday.\par    "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely leave a similar amount\par Friday, to make sure overnight rates stay low," said an\par official at a major bank.\par    The Y500 billion was much less than the amount that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has left in recent sessions, and on Wednesday,\par the key overnight rate briefly rose to 0.50%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Participants said that since Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to boost the yen on Wednesday and\par Thursday, the bank may have felt compelled to keep rates\par slightly higher.\par    -By Michiyo Seki; 813-5255-2941; mseki@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  12-18-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1839EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  38700 4077 4118 4154 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtci02r2