\par\par \b \uc2  Rubin/ \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  -3: Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Policy Moves, BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 18:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Rubin also said the U.S. welcomed Japanese proposals to strengthen the financial system and urged their hasty implementation. \par \par \uc2  'We also welcome the proposals by the Japanese authorities to strengthen the financial system and urge them to move forward quickly to implement those proposals,' Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  Rubin's comments came after Hashimoto announced Wednesday the government would include Y2 trillion of one-time income tax cuts to stimulate the economy in its supplementary budget for the fiscal year ending next March. \par \par \uc2  The ruling Liberal Democratic Party in Japan is also in the process this week of formally announcing a variety of other measures designed to jump-start the economy and stabilize the financial system. If considered effective by world financial market participants, the measures should help restore confidence in the Japanese economic system. \par \par \uc2  The yen moved higher on the news, and was then boosted further by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Selling dollars for yen, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move confirmed by Japanese government officials. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1712GMT \par \par \uc2  4225 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09qh4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\pi