\par\par \b \uc2  Sr. U.S. Treasury Official Cancels Japan Seminar Appearance \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 15:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON (AP-Dow Jones)--Assistant U.S. Treasury Secretary for International Affairs Timothy Geithner canceled Wednesday a scheduled appearance at a seminar on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy amid reported \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Geithner is among the top Treasury officials directly involved in international monetary matters, including coordination with the Federal Reserve over exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Treasury hasn't issued any immediate comment on overnight reports that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars against the Japanese yen. And it remains unclear whether the U.S. is poised to join in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including whether Geithner's absence from the Center for Strategic and International Studies seminar is an any way related to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity or \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unveiling overnight of fresh fiscal stimulus measures. \par \par \uc2  Officials generally note that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't work unless there is some fundamental shift in economic activity, or policy. It remains unclear whether Japan's latest stimulus plan marks a sufficient fundamental shift to warrant U.S. support of dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  Senior Treasury officials in recent months have voiced shared concerns with Japan over the strength of the yen. But in recent weeks Treasury officials have been silent on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales by the U.S. would be a major policy decision, if taken, analysts generally say. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. has been extremely limited and the last time the Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was in August 1995 when it bought dollars against yen to stabilize the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Since the Clinton administration took office in 1993, the Treasury has never sold dollars in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  By William Murray, 202-862-9272, e-mail: bmurray@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1440GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09pxf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
