\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Sakakibara -3: Frequently In Contact With G-7, U.S. \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 14:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japan had contacted the U.S. Federal Reserve or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other Group of Seven nations regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sakakibara merely said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is 'very frequently in contact with G-7 counterparts regarding a lot of issues.' \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said that LDP's proposal for tax and fiscal stimulus totaling about Y5 trillion would represent about 1% of Japan's gross domestic product, but that the package could push up the GDP by more than one percentage point, depending on whether the tax cuts will be consumed or saved. \par \par \uc2  'I think the measures will be positive by more than 1%,' he said, but added, 'how much of the income tax cut will be saved or consumed is difficult to say.' \par \par \uc2  In addition to Y2 trillion in income and residential tax reductions and Y840 billion in other tax cuts, the LDP has proposed about Y1 trillion in public works spending and more than Y1 trillion in front-loading spending on public works projects for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1998. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said he doesn't think the government made a mistake in implementing fiscal tightening measures this fiscal year, but said that Japan had misjudged the strength of the economy. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think me made a mistake, but in this kind of global world, things evolve rapidly,' he said, adding that Japan's economy was 'weaker than expected.' \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara declined to comment on whether the BOJ has been depositing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Japanese banks to improve those banks' Japan Premium rates. \par \par \uc2  Japan is in contact with G-7 partners on South Korea, adding that 'the Japan problem has been solved, the next problem to solve is the Korea problem,' Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  He said Japan was willing to take strong steps to resolve the South Korean situation. He didn't elaborate. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1349GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09prg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
