\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr down sharply in late Tokyo,succumbs to tax cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The dollar was down sharply by late Wednesday Tokyo trade after earlier falling by nearly six yen on the government's announcement of a special income tax cut and on dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised us," said a senior dealer at a U.S. bank. Dealers said they had expected the BOJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar were to rise above 131.60. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the morning, the dollar rose steadily to a high of 131.53 yen on the back of investor buying. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said behind the rise was speculation that the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's (LDP) economic stimulus package due later on Wednesday would include no surprises. \par \par \uc2  But a wave of selling erupted on a media report on Wednesday morning that Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto would announce an income tax cut. The dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first such action by the BOJ since August 1992, came after Hashimoto announced a one-time income tax cut of two trillion yen at a news briefing at 0130 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities confirmed there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dealers said was aimed at maximising the impact of the move. \par \par \uc2  "The authorities did take decisive measures in substantial volumes today and that caused a wave of surprising selling," the senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars intermittently from around 129 yen in the late morning and later at around 127.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ must have sold more than $1 billion against the yen on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the BOJ sold $100 million worth of dollars to his bank, while another dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to his bank twice in volumes of $100 million each. \par \par \uc2  Commenting on market talk of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday morning, Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, said: "We have taken decisive measures to cope with an excessive depreciation of the yen." \par \par \uc2  He added: "There will be no change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is conducted by the BOJ on behalf of the Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said although buying interest from Japanese investors and U.S. operators was strong, fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the dollar from rebounding. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said if the Federal Reserve joined in selling, the dollar might fall another five yen, but some others were sceptical about such a possibility. A European bank dealer said the authorities may not be happy about seeing an excessive movement such as the market saw in May. \par \par \uc2  "Sakakibara said he will take decisive action. So I think this is just the beginning," said Takao Sakoh, first vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Union Bank of Switzerland (UBS). \par \par \uc2  UBS's Sakoh said he disagreed with some views in the market that the dollar's fall had provided a good bargain-hunting opportunity. \par \par \uc2  "While the dollar was trading around 121 to 122 yen, the G7 had mentioned concerns about the yen weakness. So (the current level) is still too high for the dollar and too weak for the yen. There should be some more correction on the downside for the dollar," Sakoh said. \par \par \uc2  "I still believe that a very comfortable level for a lot of people, including financial authorities, is between 115 and 120 yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 130.72/82 yen and 1.7810/20 marks in New York on Tuesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtch00w2z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
