\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: U.S. Dollar Higher Despite Sakakibara Remark \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1997\par 03:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar is higher at midday in Tokyo Monday compared with its levels earlier in the session, despite a short-lived bout of profit-taking in the wake of a comment by Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As reported, Sakakibara said the ministry's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  'is already clear.' \par \par \uc2  Traders used the Sakakibara remark as a chance to take profits, but strong dollar buying interest kicked in quickly, pushing the dollar to a new five-and-a-half year high of Y131.25 amid concerns about the outlook for Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  The release earlier Monday of the Bank of Japan's latest quarterly business survey - the tankan - exacerbated those concerns, traders said. Some said that market participants are growing less concerned about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by monetary authorities, as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic fundamentals appear too weak to withstand a sharp rise in the yen's value. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. Economic fundmanentals point to a lower yen, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be effective at this point,' a trader at a European bank in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  'The Tankan report reflected the weakness of the Japanese economy, and based on this no one is likely to buy up yen,' the trader added. \par \par \uc2  'There are lots of dollar buy orders around the Y130.00 level,' the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Market players are keen to buy dollars on dips, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'I see deep dollar buy orders all the way down to the Y128.00 level,' a trader at a Japanese city bank said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0220 GMT (9:20 p.m. EST), the dollar was trading at Y131.17, up from Y130.78 around 0030 GMT (9:30 p.m. EST) and above Y130.35 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y130.05 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.7786, higher than DM1.7770 earlier in Tokyo and above DM1.7760 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.7632 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0251GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcf09mkw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
