\par\par \b \uc2  G-7 Watch -4: Possible To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  With The Flow? \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1997\par 13:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Likewise, the financial package \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling party has promised to unveil next week should help reassure the markets that it remains committed to supporting the banking system and ensuring that economic growth eventually picks up again in the foreseeable future. \par \par \uc2  In that event, a yen on the brink of turning up again could well prove ripe for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which always works much better when it is executed with - rather than against - the flow of market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  And, the Bank of Japan may well find it doesn't have to go it alone. \par \par \uc2  Apart from getting support from the U.S., it might also get help from the Deutsche Bundesbank, which this week criticized the strength of the dollar against the mark as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved up towards DM1.8000. \par \par \uc2  Ernst Welteke, a member of the Bundesbank's policy council, said that while there isn't any need for a rise in interest rates now, this situation could change if the dollar rises significantly. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keen to ensure that mark weakness doesn't bring inflationary import price rises. \par \par \uc2  'It's likely that we will continue to hear such comments' if the dollar continues to rise, said Ulrich Jacoby, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Genossenschaft Bank in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  ING Barings' Roberts said that although there isn't that much pressure on G-7 to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, a coordinated exercise is still possible to stop the 'relentless slow move of the dollar out of line with fundamentals.' \par \par \uc2  For the time being, though, Jacoby sees the Bundesbank hanging back. 'The Bundesbank can live with the current dollar level,' he said, adding that it will probably stick to only verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  even if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises over DM1.8000. \par \par \uc2  In Europe Thursday, the dollar was resuming its upward trend after a brief lull earlier in the week. It is up at Y129.39 from Y128.73 and at DM1.7724 from DM1.7715. \par \par \uc2  (G. Thomas Sims in Frankfurt and Takeshi Takeuchi in Tokyo contributed to this article.) \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1252GMT \par \par \uc2  1192 4208 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc409bco\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
