\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  not imminent -- economists. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Al Yoon \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the eroding yen stunted the dollar's rise on Tuesday but should not stand in the way of the snowballing trend against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Economists said a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen is not likely despite the raft of comments from senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials that warned the government is prepared to act in the name of exchange rate stability. \par \par \uc2  Because Japan must rely on a weaker domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a crutch to an otherwise ailing domestic economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now on behalf of the yen would be inappropriate, said Selig Sechzer, senior international economist at Alliance Capital Management. Further, a lack of stimulative policy actions by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  also detracts from any argument for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  "There's no significant fiscal stimulus that creates any prospect of growth in 1998...so the yen really has to get weaker than it is now," Sechzer said. It's clear exchange rates do follow fundamentals and the fundamentals suggest very loudly that the yen needs to be weaker." \par \par \uc2  Sechzer said prospects for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are very low because Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin has made it clear that U.S. officials will not try to drive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, Citicorp Securities International Economist Sandy Batten noted that -- even with probable trade friction as dollar/yen rises -- it is difficult to make a case that the weak yen has hurt the U.S. economy amid healthy growth and low unemployment. \par \par \uc2  Rubin on Monday said he shared Japan's concerns about the yen's weakness, but also that the U.S. exchange rate policy had not changed. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts contended Japan is probably more concerned with the speed of the yen's fall than the absolute level. In his comments, Vice Finance Minster for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said the MoF was concerned about the decline in the value of the yen and that an "excessive" depreciation would be counterproductive. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara also said "when the appropriate time comes, we may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent additions of massive liquidity for the Japanese banking system also seems to fly in the face of would-be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Citicorp's Batten. \par \par \uc2  "If the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is providing liquidity very generously to keep their financial system stable and at the same time goes to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and then sops it up your going to be left wondering what is the real intent of all this," Batten said. \par \par \uc2  Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  similar to that seen overnight will probably be the most-favored tool for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , economists said. MoF comments may also carry more weight as traders grow more reluctant to to bet against verbal warnings -- or take unnecessary risks -- as the year comes to a close. \par \par \uc2  "Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a full plate of problems and I don't think the yen is going to be one of their major ones," Batten said, adding that they will devote some time to make sure their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not collapse. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, economists said it would be folly to dismiss verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Sakakibara, MoF International Finance Bureau Director-General Haruhiko Kuroda and Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka. \par \par \uc2  Carl Wienberg, chief economist at High Frequency Economics, said he was dubious of an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that a warning was appropriate given Japanese officials' talk and other dollar negative comments from Bundesbank council member Reimut Jochimsen on Tuesday and Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "While it's impossible to pick out the timing of when these guys might jump in and decide they've reached the limit, we should be open to the idea that we may get a surprise at some point," Weinberg said. \par \par \uc2  ((--N.A. \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unit, 212-859-1672)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc301lal\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
