\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's Indonesia rupiah reserves stir debate. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Risa Maeda \par \uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1997\par 10:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stabilise an Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month succeeded in making at least some impact in the market, but it also posed a key question to Tokyo: Should Japan hold an Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves? \par \par \uc2  Japan sold U.S. dollars to buy the Indonesian rupiah in November, but the decision to hold a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen as less profitable, less liquid and riskier than the greenback has sparked criticism at home, economists said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "I would say it is nonsense for a nation to hold a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a developing country as a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sayuri Kawamura, senior economist at the Japan Research Institute. \par \par \uc2  Japanese and Singapore monetary authorities joined with Bank Indonesia to buy the rupiah against the dollar after the International Monetary Fund announced a rescue package for the crisis-hit nation. Later \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, has had little success. \par \par \uc2  Since the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has implied that it may take such action again, perhaps adding a second Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its growing external reserves. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if help was required. \par \par \uc2  `Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  some time ago was successful. We have been able to move exchange rates fairly significantly and we think this type of regional cooperation is very important,` said Sakakibara, who was attending a meeting of Asian finance ministers in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  Economist Kawamura said a nation with a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system had to keep a certain volume of external reserves for use in emergencies, and this meant the U.S. dollar was still the most appropriate reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is the first Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held as a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Officials say their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  met with some success in the market at the time it was carried out, although the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later resumed its slide and on Wednesday hit a new record low of 3,940 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said that holding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefits Japan by diversifying its portfolio, but others disagreed. \par \par \uc2  "If diversification is necessary, Japan should invest in more mark- or euro-based assets," said Kawamura. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japan's foreign reserves policy had changed since last month, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official said on Monday its policy centred on liquidity and safety, but that there were other issues to consider as well. \par \par \uc2  MOF had said previously that Japan's foreign reserves were invested in U.S. Treasures and other foreign bonds and bank accounts based on liquidity, safety and profitability. \par \par \uc2  In contrast to the shift in Japan's reserve policy, the Bundesbank said last month the German cental bank was still holding all of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  Takatoshi Itoh, professor at Hitotsubashi University, said holding the rupiah as a result of the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was justifiable because such buying seemed to have been based on a consensus among those involved in the IMF bail-out package. \par \par \uc2  Holding the rupiah was not against the national interest since it was bought in conjunction with IMF requirements for economic reform in Indonesia and the volume involved was reported to be limited, said Itoh, who chairs MOF's advisory panel on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial sectors. \par \par \uc2  MOF has declined to give details of the value of the joint dollar sales for the rupiah in November, but they were estimated by traders at $300 million to $500 million. \par \par \uc2  Despite depreciation in the value of its rupiah assets, Japan's external reserves rose $235 million from a month earlier to a record $228.385 billion at the end of November. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570/fax +81-3 3432-7462 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc301iey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
