\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  seen waiting to maximise  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  effect. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kanta Watanabe \par \uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be looking to maximise the impact of any dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by waiting for a chance to conduct it at the same time as big macroeconomic events, dealers and analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Such events could include an agreement expected on Wednesday between South Korea and the International Monetary Fund (IMF) on a bailout plan for that country or the announcement of economic steps by Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) expected on December 16, they said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have only a short-term impact, as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic fundamentals did not justify a sharp yen gain, they said. \par \par \uc2  "At the current dollar/yen level, some sort of action by financial authorities is likely, as the dollar's rise could gain momentum if it breaches key technical resistance at 130 yen," said Taisuke Tanaka, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "But that is unlikely to alter the yen's downtrend over the medium term," he added. The dollar rose to a five-year high of 129.33 yen in New York on Monday on growing fears that difficulties at Japanese financial institutions will have a serious impact on Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  But it was pushed lower in Tokyo on Tuesday after senior officials of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) hinted at action to check the rise. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, especially in the yen against the dollar, were not favourable, and added that Japan stood ready to act appropriately to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stability. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, told reporters in Kuala Lumpur that excessive depreciation of the yen would be counter-productive. \par \par \uc2  "We are prepared to act as appropriate to maintain stablity of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  While MOF officials have recently been verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check dollar's rise, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the dollar for yen in August 1992, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts said MOF had in the past linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with other events. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the MOF tended to do it along with announcements of macroeconomic measures," said Makoto Miyazaki, chief manager in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury division at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi (BTM). \par \par \uc2  "Overseas speculators may have been buying dollars recently on the view that Japanese authorities won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until they have prepared such measures," he added, suggesting that one opportunity for the authorities would be the announcement of the LDP's economic steps. Credit Suisse First Boston's Tanaka agreed that MOF was showing a tendency to favour \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the same time as some event, as the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself were limited. \par \par \uc2  However, he added: "The announcement of an economic package in mid-December is not a formal government event. So \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more likely to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the time of the announcement of bilateral aid to South Korea, expected after a formal IMF agreement." The Seoul government said on Tuesday that it would sign a bailout agreement with the IMF on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Mitsuzuka told reporters on Tuesday that Japan would give maximum support to South Korea once it reaches an agreement with the IMF on its economic aid programme. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could initially knock the dollar down sharply, but the dollar is likely to find support around 125 yen as the interest rate gap between Japan and the United States still favoured the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood around 128.37/42 yen as of 1037 GMT. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-9780 email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc201sve\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
