\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Safe-Haven Capital Flows To U.S. Buoy Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1997\par 23:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said there were several signs pointing to the likelihood of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, such as price checking with various central banks. The moves came one day after the dollar hit a five-year high of Y129.33 against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday. Analysts now predict \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will come about Y130.00. \par \par \uc2  Despite the early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, 'fundamentally nothing has changed,' said Dieter Bluhm, vice president at Wells Fargo in San Francisco, referring Japan's continuing economic woes which naturally produce a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  Capital flowing from Japan and other Asian markets amid the turmoil is giving the dollar additional strength against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's strength against the mark in New York was also a product of this safe-haven flow into U.S. stocks and bonds. The mark was unable to sustain gains made earlier after Bundesbank Jochimsen's comments, beaten down by turmoil in Russian and other east European markets. \par \par \uc2  Monday, the ruble suffered its sharpest one-day decline of the year after the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the ruble's trading band amid continuing concern about the health of various Russian commercial banks in the wake of the country's economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  German commercial banks, said traders are over exposed in their loan portfolios to both Russia and other countries of eastern Europe. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late Tuesday in Russia, the dollar changed hands at 5959-5960 rubles,\par unchanged from Monday, after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and an increase by the Russian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its Lombard lending rate to 36% in an effort to slow\par declines in the ruble.\par   (For a fuller account of the day's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity, please\par turn to Dow Jones page 1033)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2207GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 28038 61027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc2099g6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
