\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: German Rate Rise Seen Less Likely \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 22:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the mark was undercut by indications the Deutsche Bundesbank is less likely to raise interest rates than the market has widely believed. \par \par \uc2  First, Germany announced retail sales data that showed an annualized decline of 1% in September and betrayed an extremely soft level of domestic demand. Secondly, Klaus Dieter-Kuehbacher, president of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Berlin and a member of the Bundesbank's policy-setting council, said he hoped to see German rates stay at their current levels until EMU is launched in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  The central banker's comments were especially negative for the mark because \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had largely factored in expectations that Germany's rates would have to rise to converge with those of its prospective EMU partners. \par \par \uc2  MFR's Koss said many market participants now believe the prevailing economic conditions in Europe will prevent the Bundesbank from raising interest rates again. \par \par \uc2  'To tighten any more will be genuinely restrictive at a time of record high unemployment and just 1% inflation,' Koss said. 'What possible justication could there be for it?' \par \par \uc2  The dollar's recent rally versus the yen was halted early in Asian trading by widespread, but unconfirmed, rumors that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later recovered in Europe as traders sold the yen in the belief that a stimulus package to be released Friday by the ruling Liberal Democratic Party will disappoint the market. Later, in the day, dealers unwound those positions, and the dollar lost ground against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said that move also reflected a shift to a more optimistic view of the package's impact on Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97 \par \par \uc2  2159GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08pab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
