\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: DEM Fall Vs Yen Also Pushes Down Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 02:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y73.23, down from Y73.46 earlier and below Y73.70 in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Wednesday at Y73.36. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.7023, down from $1.7033 earlier and below $1.7045 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.7045 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  After rising to a new six-month high of Y126.60 earlier, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to an intraday low of Y125.85 on profit-taking by Japanese banks. The dollar last traded higher on May 6, when it touched Y126.82. \par \par \uc2  Selling of the mark for yen also pushed down the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But interest by Japanese importers and investors to buy on dips around Y125.80 is likely to lend support to the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a report in the Japanese newspaper Mainichi Shimbun Thursday quoting sources as saying that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell dollars for yen since last week, has caused some nervousness in the market about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'Some feel that since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is so quiet (about the dollar's rise), monetary authorities may actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no reaction to the release of Japan's September current account data, which showed that Japan's unadjusted current account surplus rose 63.7% on year to Y1,165 trillion. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Bank of Korea entered the market to sell dollars at 988 won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0116GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08ocm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
