\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF, BOJ Mulling Dlr-Selling Since Last Week - Report \b0\par\par\uc2 118 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 01:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell dollars for yen since last week, Japanese newspaper Mainichi Shimbun reported in its Thursday morning edition. \par \par \uc2  The article, quoting 'close sources,' said that because weak Japanese stock prices and the sluggish economy could make \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ineffective, the BOJ and MOF have so far not been able to find the right timing to enter the market. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ and MOF are waiting until market players take profits on long dollar positions to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the report said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0013GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08o8i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
