\par\par \b \uc2  APEC/Focus On  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -4:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  'Model' For Fund \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 10:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Some Southeast Asian countries may resist an Asia Fund that falls wholly under the control of the IMF. And the idea of including the U.S. in a regional surveillance body, when the Clinton administration is having trouble providing any money for the Asian countries in trouble, could be controversial. \par \par \uc2  Officials at Japan's Finance Ministry say they've scaled back some of their earlier plans for the Asia Fund in the face of resistance from the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Instead of a permanent fund, they may propose that Asian countries should pledge their willingness to provide emergency credit lines, similar to the IMF's facilities, in the event of a crisis. The credits would be subject to the IMF's conditions on fiscal and monetary reform - effectively acting as a supplement to the IMF's own lending. Alternatively, strong Asian countries could set up direct credit lines with the weaker economies. \par \par \uc2  But Japanese officials say even these ideas, which they may put forward at the Manila meeting, may not be acceptable to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Japanese vice minister of finance for international affairs Eisuke Sakakibara, a key player in the Asia Fund planning, is scheduled to attend the Manila meeting, as well as U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers. Deputy finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials from Australia, Brunei, China, Hong Kong, Indonesia, South Korea, Malaysia, Singapore and Thailand will also attend, as well as representatives of the IMF, World Bank and ADB. \par \par \uc2  Even if Japan is modifying its plans, Southeast Asian countries still seem intent on creating a proper fund, with Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad stressing this week that plans for such a facility are still intact. \par \par \uc2  And Philippine president Fidel Ramos has repeatedly talked about an Asia fund in the context of both APEC and ASEAN, describing it as something that 'would assure participating economies of the availability of funds and that reforms and adjustment measures are pursued.' \par \par \uc2  Dalla said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Singapore could provide a model for how an Asia fund might work. When the Bank of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore joined Bank Indonesia in buying rupiah on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this month, they weren't just trying to halt a slide in the rupiah, but trying to build confidence around Indonesia's newly-agreed IMF program. \par \par \uc2  That kind of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sewn right onto the side of an IMF package, goes to the heart of what an Asia fund might be, said Dalla. 'It will be for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' with the IMF-imposed controls acting as a 'safety net,' he said. \par \par \uc2  -By James T. Areddy; 852.2802.7002; jareddy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0905GMT \par \par \uc2  1142 4204 62551 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08ni9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
