\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr dips vs yen in late Tokyo on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0640 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     125.50/60\tab \tab 126.65-124.85\par  USD/DEM     1.7216/26\tab \tab 1.7260-1.7145\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped versus the yen in late Tokyo on Thursday as bulls were shaken by talk of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no trace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding that many operators took such talk as an excuse to take profits, as there had been concerns that the dollar may be at a level where the BOJ is eager to check its rise. \par \par \uc2  "There was talk in the early morning that the BOJ sold the dollar against the yen through U.S. banks in Singapore. But I didn't hear the bank do that and I don't think the BOJ dares to do it either," said a long-term credit bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  A feeling that the dollar has been overbought has been building since the start of trade here, partly due to a newspaper report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) and the BOJ were waiting for a good time to sell dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  The Mainichi Shimbun said on Thursday that MOF and the BOJ have been considering dollar sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was also talk of major dollar sales by a U.S. hedge fund prior to the emergence of a Japanese wire service report that the BOJ appeared to have sold dollars at the higher end of 126-127 yen in morning trade in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Although we could not confirm it, we doubt that it really took place," a bank dealer said, referring to the report. \par \par \uc2  "Profit-taking by overseas operators triggered stop-loss sales at 125.50 yen and knocked the dollar down to 125.20 yen." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said easing fears of a further sell-off in the yen, government bonds and Tokyo stocks were behind the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovery. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, concerns over Japanese stocks and financial system caused triple falls in Tokyo financial markets. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the Nikkei 225 average sustained a small loss of 0.04 percent to close at 15,427.27. But a healthy rebound in government bonds forced yen bears to amend their bets. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations still exist that Japan may come up with some effective measures in the coming weeks to stop the economy from deteriorating," said a city bank dealer. The ruling Liberal Democratic Party is due to announce a second set of economic stimulus measures on Friday. This will be followed by a government economic package on November 18. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers said the dollar's outlook remained bullish as a retreat was needed to prepare for a climb towards this year's high of 127.47 yen. Options-related stop-loss buying is expected to take place at several points up to 128.00. \par \par \uc2  Koyo Ozeki, a director of rating agency IBCA, told Reuters Financial Television on Thursday that Japan's financial system would be in a real crisis if the Nikkei were to sink to the 14,000 level, forcing Japan to take steps to protect the system. \par \par \uc2  Ozeki said that to protect the financial markets, public funds would need to be injected into the banking system soon, via Japan's deposit insurance system. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Thursday, however, that he had no intention of using public funds to resolve the issue of problem loans held by financial firms. \par \par \uc2  Mitsuzuka also said the Hong Kong G7 agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still intact, adding that Japan will deal with \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues in an appropriate and timely manner. This comment was shrugged off by the market. \par \par \uc2  Senior MOF officials on Thursday declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  - Risa Maeda Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-8570 \par \par \uc2  email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbd02lx9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
