\par\par \b \uc2  MOF says to deal appropriately with  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  -- Jiji. \b0\par\par\uc2 135 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 13 (Reuters) - Japan will deal appropriately with excessive moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the international finance bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), was quoted by Jiji news agency as saying on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda told Jiji he would not comment on market rumours that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  "Excessive moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates will be dealt with appropriately," Kuroda was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda also said that the agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  among the Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations at their meeting in Hong Kong in September was still in effect, the news agency said. \par \par \uc2  - Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-9780 \par \par \uc2  email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbd02lg9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
