\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  forging new  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fund-raising method. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tatsuo Ito \par \uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to revamp its fund-raising methods for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to better match global standards as it braces for new financial reforms -- and also to nurture its underdeveloped money market, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  But the nation's two top monetary authorities, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) and the Bank of Japan (BOJ), are said to be at odds over how such changes take place. \par \par \uc2  At issue is whether the BOJ should continue underwriting 60-day government debt financing bills, called FBs, which the Finance Ministry MOF uses to raise funds cheaply in order to buy dollars when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Not only private institutions but also the authorities will be required to make comprehensive changes as the Big Bang approaches," said Masuhisa Kobayashi, vice president at Merrill Lynch Japan. \par \par \uc2  "Japan's short-term money market is fairly immature, and without any improvements the yen would become merely a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as foreigners could be deprived of the opportunity to hold yen as reserves," he added. \par \par \uc2  Senior officials of the MOF and the BOJ are holding regular meetings to discuss the issues in the short-term money markets, including means of short-term debt underwriting by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  For decades, the BOJ has insisted that FBs, should be sold in the market rather than underwritten by the BOJ, arguing that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  involvement in financing the government debts by rolling over short-term debts could lead to inflation. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry, for its part, has resisted BOJ's calls, mainly for fear of losing flexibility in raising funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Officials at both MOF and the BOJ said nothing specific has been decided on reforming the system of funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through BOJ underwriting of FBs, and there was no timetable for any action. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said that the BOJ may try to rid itself of this long-standing yoke by taking advantage of upcoming "Big Bang" financial reforms and of BOJ law revisions in April 1998 that will give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  greater independence. \par \par \uc2  By clarifying the functions of the BOJ, the new law may give the BOJ the strength to resist government pressure to underwrite FBs, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  MOF, Japan's most powerful ministry, has traditionally set FB rates below prevailing market rates to keep fund-raising costs low. FB rates are currently 0.125 percentage point below the discount rate, which currently stands at 0.5 percent. As a result, they seldom attract private buyers and the BOJ has traditionally been expected to purchase the bulk of them. \par \par \uc2  By selling FBs at competitive rates, the government could  boost liquidity in the short-term money market and help promote the yen as a key global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Demand for short-term government securities is rising amid growing worries about risk in securities issued by private financial institutions and companies, some of which already face the threat of default due to bankrupcy. \par \par \uc2  "We would like to make FBs a core instrument of the short-term money market, alongside (Japanese) T-bills," a senior BOJ official said. \par \par \uc2  The volume of creditworthy T-bills stands at around 12 trillion yen, but the bulk of that is held by portfolio investors or foreign central banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the volume of FBs was about 30 trillion yen at the end of October. \par \par \uc2  MOF usually buys dollars for yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after raising \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen funds by issuing FBs through the ministry's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Economists said this practice deviated from that in other industrialised nations, with France and Germany banning \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of government debt as part of their preparations for a single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Sayuri Kawamura, an economist at Japan Research Institute, said there were serious problems with the way the ministry's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account functions. \par \par \uc2  "The account is questionable because MOF raises yen funds at an extremely low and fixed rate and then can invest them in higher-yielding U.S. Treasury bills, which automatically brings profits without any effort," she said. "The ministry should clarify to the public its responsibilities regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as other nations do," she added. \par \par \uc2  Market experts estimate that the Japanese government bought nearly 50 billion dollars in 1995 when it battled a steep appreciation of the yen that threatened to suffocate Japanese export business. \par \par \uc2  - Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-1396 \par \par \uc2  email:tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtba02wki\par }\pa