\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar holds gains, BOJ sidelined in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1997\par 05:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The dollar held on to substantial overnight gains in Tokyo on Thursday afternoon due to a market belief that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) will stay on the sidelines despite the greenback's rally, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment gained strength on Wednesday that the U.S. and Japanese monetary authorities will tolerate the dollar's rally, at least for a while, despite the recent Group of Seven agreement," said Hokuto Nakano, manager of the Industrial Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ltd's International Treasury Department. \par \par \uc2  Fears of possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly receded, traders said, after senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters overnight in New York, apart from saying that Japan's policy on exchange rates remains unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to a high of 123.33 yen in early Tokyo trading, up from Wednesday's New York close of 123.05/15 yen, but still short of a six-month high of 123.45 yen reached during intraday trade in New York. \par \par \uc2  The main buyers were U.S. funds, including speculative accounts, investment trusts and pension funds, traders said. \par \par \uc2  With the dollar around 122.90 by early afternoon, the BOJ still appeared content to stay on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  The dollar firmed mainly on the back of speculation that the U.S. and Japan have agreed to let the dollar firm for the time being in light of the faltering Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar-bullish market ignored comments by MOF official Haruhiko Kuroda that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement struck by the Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations in September remains intact. The G7 said in September, in an apparent reference to the yen, that excessive depreciations of exchange rates are undesirable. \par \par \uc2  Some traders warned, however, that the bullishness may not be warranted in view of the growing irritation of U.S. exporters. \par \par \uc2  A strong dollar undermines U.S. exports as it boosts prices of U.S.-made products on the global market. \par \par \uc2  The recent Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil and the deep depreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also slashing U.S. exports to Asia, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stocks were marginally lower in early afternoon trade, although the dollar's rise against the yen had given a lift to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -sensitive exporters during the morning session, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's main share index, the 225-share Nikkei average, was off 23.07 points or 0.14 percent at 16,424.98. Nikkei 225 December futures fell 10 points to 16,430. \par \par \uc2  Japanese government bonds (JGBs) were lower at midday as stronger Tokyo stocks, and a sense that Asian stock markets appear to be more settled, inhibited buying in an already factorless market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark December futures contract was at 130.67, down 0.08 from Wednesday's close. The yield of the key 182nd 10-year JGB was at 1.610 percent, up from 1.595 percent on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  - Tokyo Treasury desk (813) 3432-1396 \par \par \uc2  email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb6033yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
