\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Dlr Higher Vs Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 07:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The sterling is currently at $1.6770, up from $1.6757 in New York late Monday. The sterling was at $1.6785 in London late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said U.S. fund managers led the selling of yen against the mark amid renewed fears about the outlook for Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a Japanese city bank said news late Monday that second-tier brokerage house Sanyo Securities Co. had filed for protection rekindled concerns that things in Japan could get worse before they get better. \par \par \uc2  'There's no reason to buy yen at this point,' the trader said. He added, however, 'Exporters are still looking to sell dollars around Y122.00, so that area looks tough right now, but a clean break of that resistance would enable a move to Y122.20.' \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at supporting Indonesia's rupiah Monday likely will have only a short-term impact. \par \par \uc2  'That effect could remain for one or two weeks, but in the longer term, we need to see proof that Indonesia has the resolve to address its fundamental problems,' Inoue said. \par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, traders greeted news that the International Monetary Fund is calling for the formation of a financing facility in Asia as potentially good news further down the line. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund said Tuesday it has proposed that Asian nations create a surveillance group and a financing facility to strengthen cooperation among Asian countries in response to turmoil in regional financial markets. \par \par \uc2  'That's definitely something that would help (promote stability in the region),' said the trader at the city bank. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Asia, the dollar is slightly higher versus the rupiah. Around 0600 GMT (1:00 a.m. EST), the dollar is quoted at 3,240 rupiah, up from its trading level around 3,220 rupiah late Monday. The dollar earlier touched an intraday low of around 3,200 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Monday, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the rupiah versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0616GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb408d4s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
