\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up vs yen on Japan financial system concerns. \b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0620 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     121.71/76\tab \tab 121.92-121.22\par  USD/DEM     1.7300/10\tab \tab 1.7380-1.7284\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 4 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against the yen by late afternoon Tokyo on Tuesday, as the yen came under pressure on renewed worries about the health of Japan's financial system. \par \par \uc2  Such worries were fuelled by the collapse of second-tier brokerage firm Sanyo Securities Co Ltd, which filed for court protection from creditors on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The Sanyo news weighed on the yen. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was not panicky because troubles at Sanyo had been well-known and the stock market reacted rather calmly today," said a dealer at a long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's Nikkei 225 stock average ended up 41.16 points or 0.25 percent at 16,500.10 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to the day's high against the yen and fell to the day's low versus the mark in early afternoon, after speculative mark buying against the yen by overseas fund operators pushed the mark/yen rate above 70.10 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark's rise gained momentum after stop-loss buy orders were triggered around 70.20 yen and 70.30 yen, taking the mark/yen rate as high as 70.45 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark stood around 70.32/35 yen as of 0650 GMT, compared with around 69.88 yen in New York on late Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The mark is a main beneficiary of the financial market instability in Asia. The mark is likely to gradually rise above 71 yen, but its upside may be heavy in the near term due to profit-taking," said the long-term credit bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said options-related mark sales for the yen that had been detected last week were decreasing. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said mark buying against the yen was seen as less risky than dollar buying versus the yen, as worries about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could heighten if the greenback rises above 122 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise was capped near 122 yen by offers from Japanese exporters. There was also talk of selling interest from Japanese institutional investors around the same level. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the market was cautious about selling dollars due to concerns about tensions in the Middle East. \par \par \uc2  "Iraqi news has so far had limited impact. But people are carefully watching the situation," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Worries about the Persian Gulf situation were heightened after Iraq warned on Monday it would shoot down American U-2 spy planes, flying over its territory in support of U.N. weapons inspectors, if the United Nations did not cancel them. \par \par \uc2  News of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), Bank Indonesia and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) to defend the Indonesian rupiah on Monday had little direct impact on dollar/yen trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday confirmed that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in concert with Bank Indonesia and MAS to defend the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could head higher overnight if New York stocks continue to rise strongly later today. But judging from the weakness of Hong Kong stocks, we might not see that happen," said the trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index was down 375.53 points or 3.34 percent at 10,879.58 as of 0738 GMT, after rising as high as 11,660.97 earlier. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 121.38/48 yen and 1.7365/75 marks in New York on Monday. - Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-9780 \par \par \uc2  email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb4037z6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
