\par\par \b \uc2  Concerted dlr sales for rupiah $300-500mln - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 4 (Reuters) - The value of concerted dollar sales for the Indonesian rupiah in Singapore on Monday by the Bank of Japan (BOJ), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) and Bank Indonesia was estimated at $300 million to $500 million, senior traders said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It (the dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) came in small lots at many commercial banks, and the total would be $300-$500 million," said a senior trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The amount, although it was clearly less than $1 billion, was considered to be substantial for the rupiah market, even though its turnover had recently been boosted by speculative demand, they said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the BOJ, the MAS and Bank Indonesia may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again should the rupiah weaken beyond 3,300 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Neither the BOJ nor the MAS used the so-called `dollar-repo` arrangements which enable Indonesia to borrow dollars for the short term from Japan and Singapore by selling from its holdings of U.S. Treasury securities with a promise to buy them back later. \par \par \uc2  A dollar repo pact was established in April 1996 and comprises nine Asian central banks, including those of Japan, Indonesia and Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 3,212.00/3,222.00 to the dollar at 0342 GMT, compared with the New York close of 3,205. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rallied on Monday to a high of 3,255 to the dollar from the opening of around 3,540/55 due to concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ, MAS and Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said in a statement on Monday that the three monetary authorities agreed they would be ready to act in the market as and when necessary in the future. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's participation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's position to support Indonesia and we hope that it will bring about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability," Mitsuzuka said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ does not comment on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-8676 \par \par \uc2  email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb4037p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
