\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firmer but capped at around 121.80 yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 4 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2  0004 GMT --*Dollar firmer against yen but capped at around 121.80 yen due to Japanese exporter offers near 122 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Earlier, Japanese investor buying and expectations of commercial dollar buying after three-day weekend lifted dollar against yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Renewed worries about Japan's financial institutions after Sanyo Securities filed for court protection on Monday and recovery in U.S. stocks helped dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  *Mark buying against yen supporting dollar/yen indirectly, with talk that options-related mark sales waning. \par \par \uc2  *"Yen (Japan's) problems are again in the spotlight after the bankruptcy of Sanyo Securities," said a European bank dealer. "The yen is not a good \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy," he added. \par \par \uc2  *Second-tier brokerage Sanyo failed after nine top life insurers said on Friday they would not extend payment periods on subordinated loans. Failure is first by a brokerage in postwar Japan. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said yen likely to be sold particularly against mark after most options-related positions that had checked mark's rise expired last Friday. \par \par \uc2  *Mark rose as high as around 70.27 yen in early trade. \par \par \uc2  *Mark around 70.16 yen at 0024 GMT. City bank dealer saw chance of mark's rise to 71 yen. \par \par \uc2  *After dipping below 69.00 overnight, dealers found mark/yen too cheap to resist, scooping up cross from around 69.15 in New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  *Japanese life insurers and trust banks may continue to sell dollars against yen on rises in bid to lock in profits on foreign securities, sales partly aimed at covering losses in their stock holdings. \par \par \uc2  *A trust bank said dollar on upward trend again after falling from recent high of around 123.05 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Separately, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday confirmed that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in concert with Indonesian and Singaporean monetary authorities to defend Indonesia rupiah. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said such action would not have direct impact on dollar/yen trade in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  *Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Tuesday he hopes \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's participation in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to help shore up the Indonesian rupiah will bring about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability.Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-1396; email:tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  "Earlier, we thought that options-related orders had already expired last week, but it seems that they are still there at 70.50 yen," a commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "There are no strong selling orders below 70.50 yen so the mark could test that level later in the day," he added. \par \par \uc2  After dipping below 69.00 overnight, dealers found the mark/yen too cheap to resist, scooping up the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from around 69.15 in New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 0345 GMT, the mark stood at 70.20/23 yen after closing at 69.88 yen in New York on Monday. The Tokyo market was closed for a holiday on Monday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb4037my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
