\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Sterling Up After Brown Weekend Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par 22:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Brown's comments also sparked pound buying for marks. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the pound was trading at DM2.9098, up from DM2.8881 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Speaking on the BBC television program 'Breakfast with Frost,' Brown said: 'Of course every country wants exchange rate stability, and that's what we want and I want a strong independent pound over the medium term, but the idea that we want to re-enter the ERM is wrong.' \par \par \uc2  Britain left the ERM in 1992; it's unclear if re-joining will be a precondition for entry into the European common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Last week, Brown said it would be unrealistic to join a single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the next election, which could be as late as 2002. \par \par \uc2  The U.K. purchasing managers' index for October rose to 53.7 from 52.7 in September, the PMI's highest level in six months. However, analysts doubt either the data or money supply statistics also released Monday will be a focus at the Bank of England's monetary policy commmittee meeting this week. Few believe the BOE will be raise interest rates following last week's market turmoil. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Indonesia, Singapore and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexed their muscle in an orchestrated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which successfully pushed the Indonesian rupiah sharply higher. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the Bank of Japan, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore purchased as much as $1 billion of rupiah, lifting the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was trading at 3,207.5 rupiah, down from 3,270.50 rupiah late in Asian trading and sharply down from 3,605 rupiah at Friday's close in Asia. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-11-97 \par \par \uc2  2145GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb308byi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
