\par\par \b \uc2  REPEAT:Singapore's MAS/Indonesia -2:Aim To Strengthen Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par 06:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--Singapore's Finance Ministry said in a statement that the central banks of Singapore, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly Monday in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy rupiah against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In a brief note from Finance Minister Richard Hu, the statement said, 'This joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflects our confidence in the macroeconomic policies of the Indonesian government.' \par \par \uc2  'The depreciation of the rupiah in recent months is excessive. Today's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at promoting a strengthening of the rupiah to levels more consistent with the fundamentals of the Indonesian economy,' the statement said. \par \par \uc2  The central banks involved were the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, The Bank of Japan and Bank of Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0506GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb308bne\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
