\par\par \b \uc2  Japan sending warnings on further yen fall-traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 9 (Reuter) - Japanese monetary authorities are sending verbal warnings to major dollar investors against a further fall of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of beyond 123 yen to the dollar, traders and investors said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  These investors include foreign speculative accounts, the Japanese public and private investors, they said. \par \par \uc2  There was also talk in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that Southeast Asian public funds were among a group of investors contacted by the Japanese authorities, they said. \par \par \uc2  "A senior official (of the monetary authorities) has recently made clear that if the dollar rises to 123 yen, it would put the brake on a further yen depreciation through dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , " said one major Japanese investor, who declined to be identified. \par \par \uc2  A fall in the dollar of nearly one yen in late Asian hours on Wednesday was prompted by large-lot dollar sales by a foreign speculative fund which was informed of the Japanese plans for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or any other specific attempts to influence exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  The market keenly watches for verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it fears could be followed by actual dollar sales by the BOJ, traders said. \par \par \uc2  This is because the market is now holding large overbought positions in the dollar against the yen -- an environment in which the BOJ's dollar selling can be most effective. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of the MOF's International Finance Bureau, told Reuters he thinks markets are aware of the G7 statement. \par \par \uc2  The G7 nations agreed in late September on the importance of avoiding excessive depreciation of key exchange rates that could lead to the re-emergence of large external imbalances. \par \par \uc2  G7 officials later said their reference to key exchange rates specifically meant the dollar/yen rate. A weaker yen against the dollar helps boost Japanese exports. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.79/89 yen at 0853 GMT on Thursday, compared with Wednesday's New York close of 121.05/10 and Tokyo close 122.24/27 yen. \par \par \uc2  -Tokyo Treasury Desk (813)-3432-8676 email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta901hjt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
