\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar seen capped above 122 yen in Asia. \b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 6 (Reuter) - The dollar is likely to be capped above 122 yen on Monday due to caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), and activity is seen centring on mark/yen cross trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar/yen rate is reaching alarming levels," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese city bank dealer also said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take place if the dollar rises close to 123 yen. \par \par \uc2  But both said there would be no good reasons to keep buying the yen, with the market little concerned about Japan's trade surplus and U.S.-Japan trade friction. \par \par \uc2  The trust bank dealer said the dollar rose as high as around 122.43 yen in New York on Friday, following mark/yen buying and weaker-than-expected U.S. September job data. \par \par \uc2  Growing tension over the Middle East also helped boost the dollar against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The trust bank dealer said despite concern over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there was not a perception that the dollar has hit its upside. "There could be a chance the dollar will cautiously rise to 123 yen this week," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is likely to find short-term support at around 121.50 yen in Asia on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) will release Japan's trade data for the first 20-days of September on Monday. U.S. and Japanese trade negotiators are set to meet on October 8-9 in San Francisco to review a 1995 auto trade agreement. \par \par \uc2  Previously these factors tended to serve as yen buying factors, but traders said they were no longer focusing on trade-related issues. "Nothing special is likely to come out of the U.S.-Japan car review," said the Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  He said trade would mainly be driven by mark/yen this week, with a rise to 70 yen likely due to growing expectations of higher German interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The city bank dealer also said he would focus on whether the dollar will fall below key support of 1.75 marks. \par \par \uc2  Weak U.S. job data on Friday raised expectations that the Federal Reserve will keep interest rates steady through the end of this year, which gave support to the dollar against the mark. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers said the dollar could hit its near-term floor against the mark at the 1.75 mark level. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo treasury desk 81-3-3432-1396 \par \par \uc2  email:tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta501hy3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
