\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Wary Of Dlr-Selling  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1997\par 08:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark is quoted at Y66.08, down from  Y66.27 in New York late Tuesday and below Y66.30 in London late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at US$1.5919, up from US$1.5915 in New York late Tuesday. Sterling was at US$1.5885 in London late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said economic fundamentals were still stacked up in favor of buying dollars against the yen, and most characterized Wednesday's fall as a temporary correction. \par \par \uc2  'Looking at present situation objectively, it's overwhelmingly advantageous to buy dollars,' said Masafumi Kurokawa, first vice president at First National Bank of Chicago in Tokyo. He said that the dollar could rise as high as Y123.50 this week, after it tests the low-Y120.00 level. \par \par \uc2  But market players are wary that U.S. officials may step up its protests if Japan's trade surplus continues to rise sharply, which is possible if the yen continues to weaken. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers even see dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a possibility ahead of the meeting of Group of Seven industrialized countries' finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors on Sept. 20. \par \par \uc2  Kurokawa said that there were vague market rumors Tuesday that the BOJ was ready to sell dollars at Y122.00. A report in the Nikkei financial daily Tuesday that quoted Tomomitsu Oba, a former top Finance Ministry official as suggesting that dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a possibility, also caused market cautiousness, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But for the near-term, dollar-buying interest by Japanese investors on dips, especially at the low-Y120.00 level, will limit the dollar's fall, they said. \par \par \uc2  'The loss-cutting is mostly by short-term players like interbanks and trading companies. Longer-term players are still likely to sell yen,' Sanwa's Hashimoto said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-09-97 \par \par \uc2  0636GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9306flv\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 17/10/1999\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\